\paragraph{Why not flow-matching velocity divergence (FMVD)?}
An alternative uncertainty signal is the divergence of the flow-matching velocity field, which measures local ``turbulence'' in the generative ODE~\cite{lipman2023flow}. We find FMVD uncorrelated with action-space variance ($\rho{=}0.08$): the ODE-space signal captures generative complexity rather than action uncertainty. This negative result confirms that action-space signals are necessary for adaptive $K$ allocation.

\paragraph{Inference summary.}
At each control step, the pipeline: (1) draws $K{=}2$ action chunks from the frozen VLA, (2) computes $d_2$, (3) if $d_2 > \tau$, extends to $K{=}10$ with argmin selection and CRM correction; otherwise uses the $K{=}2$ mean, and (4) executes the first action of the output chunk before re-planning. CRM inference adds ${\sim}$0.25\,ms; the VLA forward pass (${\sim}$170\,ms batched) dominates latency.

